# Cloudflare Pages security headers.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
# This file is copied verbatim into the build output (out/) and applied by
# Cloudflare's edge. It has NO effect on GitHub Pages — it's Cloudflare-only.
#
# Most specific path wins. The Content-Security-Policy is shipped in
# Report-Only mode first so it can't break the GoHighLevel chat widget, hosted
# forms, or GA before it's been validated against real traffic. Once the
# browser console / CSP report endpoint shows no violations, rename the header
# from `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` to `Content-Security-Policy` to
# enforce it.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.leadconnectorhq.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://*.leadconnectorhq.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://images.unsplash.com https://*.leadconnectorhq.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.leadconnectorhq.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com; frame-src 'self' https://*.leadconnectorhq.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://*.leadconnectorhq.com; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# NOTE on the builder embeds (/embed/*): they're framed same-origin by our own
# product pages, which the global `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` + CSP
# `frame-src 'self'` already allow — so no override is needed here. (An earlier
# /embed/* rule that set `X-Frame-Options: ALLOWALL` produced a SECOND, conflicting
# X-Frame-Options header, which browsers reject → the iframe showed "refused to
# connect".) If third-party partner embedding is ever required, drop X-Frame-Options
# globally and control framing with CSP `frame-ancestors` per-path instead.
